WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.200 --> 00:05.280
Your physical presence is fundamental to the way you connect to an audience.

2
00:06.310 --> 00:14.630
If the way you stand, the way you look, the way you move doesn’t support your message, it will distract and detract from your message.

3
00:17.380 --> 00:25.310
Think about how you feel when a speaker says, “I’m very excited about the new plan.” You don’t believe them.

4
00:26.210 --> 00:28.100
We’re expert at reading body language.

5
00:29.130 --> 00:32.300
So take the time before you speak to prepare yourself physically.

6
00:32.330 --> 00:36.670
You wouldn’t run onto the sports field without warming up.

7
00:37.350 --> 00:43.750
You shouldn’t step onto a podium, or step up in a meeting, without preparing physically as well.

8
00:44.330 --> 00:53.630
What do we mean by physical presence? We mean that combination of body language, of stance, of expression, of gesture

9
00:54.250 --> 01:01.670
that sends signals to an audience about whether a speaker is confident, whether they’re relaxed, whether they’re credible.

10
01:02.850 --> 01:10.560
These messages, these unspoken physical messages, have enormous power to influence how an audience reacts to us.

11
01:11.170 --> 01:14.790
They can undercut our message, however well crafted our words are.

12
01:15.140 --> 01:20.710
If we aren’t backing that up with a dynamic, energised, confident physical presence,

13
01:21.090 --> 01:26.560
we’re going to lose the audience. It’s also quite hard, though, because the last thing you want when you’re presenting

14
01:27.170 --> 01:31.110
is to have part of your being going, “Oh dear, am I fiddling with my fingers?”

15
01:31.720 --> 01:36.100
And it’s really hard to communicate powerfully if you’re worrying in those ways.

16
01:36.840 --> 01:44.770
So actually the best way to get rid of those physical distractions is by grounding yourself well in advance.

17
01:45.770 --> 01:51.010
So feet nice and firmly on the floor. Take some deep breaths in.

18
01:51.940 --> 01:56.070
Think about calming things that can ground and centre you.

19
01:57.290 --> 02:08.740
Those kinds of techniques, just before you go in to present or be in a workshop or a meeting, can really help give your physical presence more groundedness

20
02:09.090 --> 02:14.750
and avoid those little distractions. I’m not saying we all have to look

21
02:15.270 --> 02:21.280
like a Hollywood actor. We all have our own way of being present. And that’s the important thing you need to do:

22
02:21.930 --> 02:26.180
find out what your natural style is, and be confident within it.

